 2. 🥇 Summer Olympics windfall 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios The 2028 Summer Olympics could generate over $40 billion and create nearly a quarter-million jobs, the L.A. Times reports from a new analysis. 

 Those are the high-end figures in a report conducted for LA28, the organizing committee behind the Los Angeles Games. 🌹 The report's less-rosy scenarios put increased economic output at around $20 billion–$25 billion, or $35 billion–$40 billion.

 Reality check: Pre-Olympics estimates have a history of overstating the Games' economic payoff — sometimes dramatically so.

 One projection ahead of the 2024 Paris Olympics called for $12.8 billion in net economic benefits. The actual result: just $2.3 billion. Go deeper . 

 
 
