 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Tony Powell 👩‍💼 Kristen Silverberg, a policy expert and former ambassador, was named the new president and CEO of Business Roundtable, the top policy voice of America's leading CEOs. Silverberg, now BRT's COO, will succeed Josh Bolten , a former White House chief of staff who has led the organization for the past decade , when he steps down Jan. 31. Go deeper . 🏦 The Federal Reserve raised interest rates a quarter point — and hinted that another rate hike is on the way this year. More from Axios' Neil Irwin . 📄 Charlie Kirk's family blamed Utah officials for failing to prevent the conservative activist's assassination, filing a wrongful death notice that presages a possible lawsuit. Get the latest . 🎙️ Tech journalists and former "Hard Fork" hosts Kevin Roose and Casey Newton are starting a new NPR show about AI. "Machine Gods" will launch in October as a twice-weekly, video-first show about the consumer, enterprise and policy implications of AI. The show will be built for YouTube but also distributed as a podcast, with one episode focusing on interviews and another on news and analysis, Newton told Axios. NPR plans to bring the show to radio in early 2027. Go deeper . 
 
